jobs.description:
To strengthen our Supply Chain Department we are looking for a LOGISTICS TEAM LEADER:

Safran Aircraft Engine Services Brussels is a subsidiary of Safran Aircraft Engines, based at Brussels Airport (Zaventem & Steenokkerzeel, Belgium), specialized in the inspection, maintenance and repair (MRO) of the advanced LEAP jet engines that power the latest generation of the Airbus A320NEO & Boeing B737MAX narrow body families. The company is a key player in the integrated CFM international MRO network. With more than 75 years of experience, and up to 20 international Part 145 certifications (EASA/ FAA/ CAAC/ …), Safran Aircraft Engine Services Brussels is recognized as a worldwide center of expertise in the air transport industry. More than a 100 airlines, lessors, private aircraft operators and MRO partners have entrusted their engines to our company. We employ over 500 highly skilled, passionate and enthusiastic employees.

Your role:

• You are a point of contact for our transport partners;
• You lead a team of 10 logistics colleagues;
• You provide support for your team by developing their knowledge in cooperation with your manager;
• You propose relevant KPI's and create reports for the activity;
• You lead the daily activity meeting together with your manager;
• You follow the work and safety instructions specifically to the workstation and the company;
• You respect the internal quality regulations and the rules of logistics and administrative management of the company;
• You inspire and enthuse employees and stimulate teamwork;
• You take initiatives and make proposals in a context of continuous improvement, pro-actively evaluates, coordinates the improvement of current work methods and introduces new technologies as they arise;
• You maintain constructive and effective relations within and outside the company.

Your profile:

• You hold at least a Bachelor in Supply Chain or Logistics, or a technical education in Logistics with experience, or you have demonstrated experience as a Team Leader;
• You have at least 5 years of experience in team management;
• You demonstrate good communication skills, good practical sense and a sense of initiative while anticipating and taking part in the context of continuous improvement;
• You have a good team spirit and are open and adaptable;
• You speak Dutch, French and are fluent in English;
• You have a good knowledge of IT tools (MS Office + ERP). SAP is a plus

Candidates must be legally authorized to work in Belgium, holding either an EU passport or a valid work & residence permit. Please note that we do not provide assistance with visa or permit applications.
